  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "2y1pplm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PRIME MINISTER AND COUNCIL OF MINISTERS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 74 mandates a Council of Ministers headed by the Prime Minister to aid and advise the President.",
        "Article 75 governs the appointment, oath, tenure, qualifications, and salaries of the Prime Minister and other Ministers.",
        "The Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the Lok Sabha, upholding the parliamentary form of governance.",
        "Ministers hold office during the pleasure of the President, representing the principle of individual responsibility.",
        "The Cabinet acts as the core decision-making executive body within the broader Council of Ministers."
      ],
      "id": "occslxk"
    },
